.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include "myfilefunctions.h"

int wordCount(FILE *file, int *lines, int *words, int *chars);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B wordCount()
function reads the file stream pointed to by
.I file
from its current position to end of file, and stores the number of
lines, words and characters into
.IR lines ", " words " and " chars
respectively.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or \-1 on failure (for example, if any pointer
argument is NULL).
